@@ -1184,6 +1186,34 @@ These limits are approximate, so `vmagent` can underflow or overflow them by a s
 
 See also [cardinality explorer docs](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/single-server-victoriametrics/#cardinality-explorer).
 
+## Limiting the number of targets per job
+
+Service discovery mechanisms backed by an external source (Kubernetes API, cloud provider API, Consul, a custom
+catalog served via `http_sd_configs`, etc.) occasionally return an excessive number of targets because of
+a misconfiguration on the discovery side (for example, a label or tag filter is accidentally removed, or
+a catalog query becomes too broad). By default `vmagent` scrapes every discovered target, so such an incident
+can spike memory and CPU usage and degrade scraping for every other job running on the same `vmagent` instance.
+
+`vmagent` can enforce an upper bound on the number of active scrape targets a single job (`job_name`) is
+allowed to have at once, regardless of which service discovery mechanism supplied the targets:
+
+* Via `max_scrape_targets` config option at [scrape_config](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#scrape_configs) section.
+  This limit applies on a per-job basis.
+* Via `max_scrape_targets` option at the `global` section of `-promscrape.config`. This sets a default limit
+  for all the scrape jobs, which don't explicitly set their own `max_scrape_targets`.
+
+By default, `max_scrape_targets` is disabled (set to `0`), so existing setups aren't affected.
+
+If a job discovers more targets than the configured `max_scrape_targets`, then only the first `max_scrape_targets`
+of them are scraped, while the rest are excluded from scraping. `vmagent` doesn't crash or reject the whole job
+in this case. The excluded targets are registered as dropped targets with the `max_scrape_targets` reason, so
+operators can notice and investigate the issue using the usual places for checking scrape target health:
+
+* The `/targets` page shows a warning banner for every job which currently exceeds its `max_scrape_targets` limit,
+  together with the number of excluded targets.
+* The `/service-discovery` page and `/api/v1/targets` API lists the excluded targets among the dropped targets,
+  with `max_scrape_targets` as the drop reason.
+
 ## Monitoring
 
 `vmagent` exports various metrics in Prometheus exposition format at `http://vmagent-host:8429/metrics` page.
